proposals.what:
On #review, above the grid, a row of toggle chips with counts: Unanswered 5 · For review 3 · Guesses 2 (Guesses only when confidence tags are on). The default is Unanswered plus For review. Next to them is the pill "Go through 8" (Enter). Queue order: unanswered by position ascending (modules run easiest first, so early blanks are the cheapest points), then marked, then guesses. In queue mode:
- the footer centre reads "Going through · 3 of 8 · Q14 ⌃";
- Next and → go to the next queued question, and Back to the previous one;
- queued strip segments get a ring;
- a quiet "Stop" returns to #review.
Answering a blank or unmarking a question updates the tiles live. Next on the last queued question returns to #review with the toast "Done: 5 answered, 2 unmarked". Anywhere in a module, U jumps to the next unanswered question and Shift+M to the next marked one, wrapping around; both are listed in the ? sheet (both keys are free in the runner map). The navigator's footer gets the same "Go through 8" beside "Go to review page". On a phone the pill is full width in the footer. Step count to revisit 8 questions: on TopTierPrep, each takes a cell click, the answer, opening the navigator and 'Go to Review Page', so 24 extra taps. Ours takes 1 pill and 8 Nexts, or on the keyboard Shift+R, Enter, then A–D and →.

The uniform pace (elapsed ÷ 95 s) is replaced by a budget per position. Budget = tier base × personal factor, normalised so the module adds up to its duration minus a check reserve (3:00 for a 35:00 module, scaled by the timing factor). Tier bases are the student's median ms on first-try right answers per tier in timed sittings and timed practice (attempts, at least 15 per tier). Otherwise defaults apply: easy 60 s, medium 95 s, hard 135 s. Each slot's tier comes from the form's public ladder (blueprint.TIERS counts, sorted), which is the same for every sitting of that form, never from the items served, so nothing about the actual questions leaks. The payload adds pace {budget_s[22], reserve_s, source 'you'|'default', n}. With Pace guide on:
- the strip's tick sits at the question you should be on;
- under the clock, a DM Mono line reads "+1:20 ahead" or "0:45 behind", updated every 5 s, in ink and never red;
- Check your work shows "Keep 3:00 for checking";
- Between modules shows "At Q11 you were 2:10 behind".
The lobby row reads "Pace guide · paced to your speed (212 timed answers)" with Change: Off / Even / Ladder. P2 judges front-loaded time against the same budgets.
